1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:08,000
94 of the last 100 launches locked none of their liquidity.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:16,000
A floor computed before the first public trade, verifiable by anyone.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:23,200
We sold every token holders had.

4
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:28,000
The worst fill of the whole sell-out: 0.998 × the floor, fees included.

5
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,160
Buyers trade on the Dynamic Bonding Curve.

6
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,960
85% migrates into DAMM v2: two positions, permanently locked, owned by the program.

7
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:52,480
15%, the migration fee, rests as one DLMM limit order at the floor price F.

8
00:00:52,480 --> 00:01:02,000
Three Meteora products. Remove one, and there is no floor.

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:10,000
The floor is recorded on-chain in the launch transaction, before anyone else can trade.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:18,000
The worst case becomes a number you know before you buy.

11
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:35,280
The price slides down the pool's curve, lands on the floor, and the bid absorbs the rest.

12
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:42,000
Every fill is burned, so the floor ends higher than it started.

13
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:54,960
Don't trust our app: one command recomputes everything from raw accounts. 16 checks.

14
00:01:54,960 --> 00:02:06,000
And one command works on mainnet today, on any Meteora pool.

15
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:21,000
The page: your worst case, verified in your browser, with redemption at F less 0.5%.

16
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:36,000
One config and one instruction for a launchpad. Tested against Meteora's mainnet binaries.

17
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Not on mainnet yet. Not audited. Late buyers can lose about 74%.

18
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Ballast. Launch with a floor.
